<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 6th century BCE</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 500s BCE: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 550 BCE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10519 5536" role="img" aria-label="Map: 6 numbered states of the world in 550 BCE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="6140" cy="1251" r="179"/><text x="6140" y="1326" font-size="215">1</text></g><g><circle cx="7909" cy="1324" r="179"/><text x="7909" y="1399" font-size="215">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5591" cy="1068" r="179"/><text x="5591" y="1143" font-size="215">3</text></g><g><circle cx="6237" cy="1859" r="179"/><text x="6237" y="1934" font-size="215">4</text></g><g><circle cx="2871" cy="2792" r="179"/><text x="2871" y="2867" font-size="215">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7266" cy="1513" r="179"/><text x="7266" y="1588" font-size="215">6</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 550 BCE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Chavín &middot; Athens &middot; State of Chu &middot; Kingdom of Saba &middot; Achaemenid Empire &middot; Kingdom of Magadha</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Darius's Scythian campaign</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Pelusium</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of An</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Bi</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Thymbra</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Boju</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Cyrus the Great</li><li>Confucius</li><li>Jeremiah</li><li>Thales of Miletus</li><li>Pythagoras</li><li>Gelon</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 540–478 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 570 – c. 495 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 650–570 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 624–546 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>551–479 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 600–530 BCE</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Daric</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Hebrew</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 500s BCE, 69 recorded states were founded and 23 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Achaemenid Empire, the State of Chu and the State of Qin. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 6th century BCE, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/6th-century-bce. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 6th century BCE</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Achaemenid Empire <span>559 BCE – 330 BCE</span></li><li>State of Chu <span>1030 BCE – 223 BCE</span></li><li>Athens <span>900 BCE – 86 BCE</span></li><li>Kingdom of Saba <span>800 BCE – 275 CE</span></li><li>Chavín <span>950 BCE – 400 BCE</span></li><li>Kingdom of Magadha <span>600 BCE – 345 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Bi <span>597 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of An <span>589 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Thymbra <span>546 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Pelusium <span>525 BCE</span></li><li>Darius's Scythian campaign <span>513 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Boju <span>506 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Cyrus the Great <span>6: c. 600–530 BCE</span></li><li>Confucius <span>5: 551–479 BCE</span></li><li>Jeremiah <span>3: c. 650–570 BCE</span></li><li>Thales of Miletus <span>4: c. 624–546 BCE</span></li><li>Pythagoras <span>2: c. 570 – c. 495 BCE</span></li><li>Gelon <span>1: c. 540–478 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Daric</dt><dd>The daric was a gold coin of the Achaemenid Empire, introduced under Darius I.</dd><dt>Hebrew</dt><dd>Hebrew is a Semitic language, the language of the Hebrew Bible and of ancient Israel.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
